\[
\frac{n!}{n_1! \cdot n_2! \cdot \ldots \cdot n_k!}
\]

where \( n \) is the total number of letters, and \( n_1, n_2, \ldots, n_k \) are the counts of each repeated letter. For the word "ELLIPSE," this becomes:

\[
\frac{7!}{2! \cdot 2!}
\]

