Suzanne walks four miles every third day. To determine the fewest number of miles she can walk in February, we need to consider the number of days in February. February typically has 28 days (non-leap year) or 29 days (leap year). 

In both cases, the number of days she walks is calculated by finding the multiples of three within the month. For 28 days:
- The multiples of three are 3, 6, 9, ..., 27.
- This results in 9 days.

For 29 days:
- The multiples of three are 3, 6, 9, ..., 27.
- This also results in 9 days.

Thus, in both 28 and 29 days, Suzanne walks on 9 days. Each day she walks 4 miles, so the total number of miles she walks is:
\[ 9 \times 4 = 36 \text{ miles} \]

Therefore, the fewest number of miles Suzanne can walk in February is \(\boxed{36}\).  7%|▋         | 29/400 [1:00:26<15:29:16, 150.29s/it]
